Remember, the `OLD(variable_name)` syntax is used to refer to the value of a variable at the beginning of the function. For example, if `x` is a variable and it is used before line, you should write `OLD(x)` to make sure the function still acts correctly even if it uses `x` on the following lines. Likewise, `RET` variable is used to refer to the return value of the function in the assert statement.

